# Project Rules

## CRITICAL: Documentation Files
- NEVER create .md files in the project root or documentation folders
- NEVER write markdown documentation like README.md, GUIDE.md, etc.
- If documentation is needed, provide it ONLY in chat responses
- Exception: .specify/ and specs/ folders are allowed to have .md files (Specify system files)
- Exception: Can read existing .md files if needed

## Secrets
- NEVER include example credentials, passwords, or API keys in any files
- NEVER commit sensitive configuration
- Always use placeholder text like "YOUR_PASSWORD_HERE" if examples are absolutely needed in chat

## Git
- Always check what files are staged before committing
- Follow user instructions exactly regarding what to commit

